WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.000
c. AD 200 · Fields on Llandough hill,
above the River Ely

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:09.438
[in Welsh] See the smoke over the brow?
They've lit the fires at the stone house.

3
00:00:09.478 --> 00:00:14.530
[in Welsh] Good spelt this year, dry
enough to thresh before the rain comes.

4
00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:19.690
[in Welsh] Thresh it quick, then. The
quern's hungry, and the children.

5
00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:24.930
[in Welsh] Fine red pots from far off, and
still the same porridge in them.

6
00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.780
[in Welsh] Gran used to say her people
kept a round house right here.

7
00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.610
[in Welsh] Now it's the barn and the oxen.

8
00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:57.427
[in Welsh] Call them in, then. There's
cloud coming up off the marsh.

9
00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:01.255
[in Welsh] And the geese are fat this
year: one for the turn of the year,

10
00:01:01.295 --> 00:01:04.715
[in Welsh] one for your mother, or we'll
never hear the end of it.

11
00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:09.970
[in Welsh] Let them run. The hill's big
enough for all of us.
